HST Office: upstream Sheets unit tests expect HST's formula conventions.

The changed expectations follow hst-sheets-excel-formula-conventions.patch (UI names CEILING/FLOOR for
the .xlsx functions, CEILING.ODF/FLOOR.ODF, FORMULATEXT, SKEW.P, FORECAST.ETS(.CONFINT/.STAT); error
cells show #VALUE!/#NUM!/... instead of Err:5xx), hst-calc-vietnamese-category.patch (category
"Vietnamese" after "Add-in") and hst-sheets-num-errors.patch (numbers outside a function's domain are
#NUM!: DATEDIF with the start after the end, GCD/LCM of a negative number, RRI, no convergence; type
errors and wrong parameter counts stay #VALUE!). Only expected values change, no test is removed.
The OpenCL suites (CppunitTest_sc_opencl-*) are not run for HST: Sheets never computes formulas with
OpenCL (hst-sheets-error-parity.patch).

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: CppunitTest_sc_ucalc, CppunitTest_sc_ucalc_formula2, CppunitTest_sc_ucalc_copypaste,
CppunitTest_sc_uicalc2, CppunitTest_sc_financial_functions_test.
